[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/main/docs/assets/brand/banner.png[/img][/center]

[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Mod Night City in JavaScript. Draw web pages over the game. Call any game function.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]REDnode is a modding framework for Cyberpunk 2077 that runs Node.js mods beside the game, draws HTML windows and HUD widgets on top of it, and gives every mod the whole game API, typed from the game's own data. It comes with an AI assistant that can write a mod with you, run it in the game and fix it.[/size][/center]

[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: PREVIEW[/color][/b][/size]
REDnode is built in the open and tested in the game after every phase, on game version 2.31. Everything on this page works in the game today. It is a preview: the API can still change between versions, and some parts (listed in the roadmap) are still to come.
[b]Players:[/b] install REDnode when a mod you want needs it.
[b]Modders:[/b] start with the [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/overlay-apps.html]guide[/url]; your first mod is one folder and one file.[/quote]
[line]
Make all kinds of screen apps, widgets, with true transparency even.
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792177505-2048305127.png[/img]

Easy to use mod manager for REDnode apps and mods (think of these like CET mods).
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792177505-1995929837.png[/img]

Full 3D, in-game editor called EDGEbuilder.
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792177511-1467588338.png[/img]

Choose from 3 different themes, including this HUD red theme like the game's UI.
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792177511-1847338957.png[/img]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What REDnode is[/color][/b][/size]

REDnode is built by [url=https://edgemodders.ai/]EDGEmodders[/url], a modding community whose idea is simple: [b]anyone can mod[/b]. Cyberpunk modding has always meant C++, redscript or Lua. REDnode adds the language most people already know, JavaScript (and TypeScript), with npm and the web's tools for making interfaces.

It has three parts, all in this download:

[list]
[*][b][color=#19f3ff]The plugin[/color][/b], a RED4ext plugin inside the game. It draws the overlay on the game's own frame, takes the mouse and keyboard when you open it (F10), and runs game calls on the game thread, safely.[/*]
[*][b][color=#19f3ff]The overlay host[/color][/b], a small app beside the game that the plugin starts and stops with it. It renders the windows and runs each Node mod in its own process, so a mod that breaks cannot take the game, or the other mods, down with it.[/*]
[*][b][color=#19f3ff]The rednode package[/color][/b], the API that mods and apps import: the game, windows, sound, TweakDB, the world, the AI assistant and more.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Highlights[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Web pages over the game[/color][/b][/size]
Any HTML page can be a window in the game: drag it, resize it, roll it up, close it. HUD widgets stay on screen while you play, hide themselves in menus, photo mode and scenes, and let clicks pass through their transparent parts. Pages are shared with the game on the GPU, so the overlay costs little (the [b]Perf[/b] sample shows exactly how much).

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]The whole game API, typed[/color][/b][/size]
[b]api[/b] calls any game function by name: global functions, static functions and the methods of game objects. It is typed from the game's own reflection data, so your editor completes every class, method and enum value in the game. The same data is published as a browsable [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/game/]game API reference[/url].

[code]import { api, game } from 'rednode';

const player = await api.GetPlayer(game.instance);
const shop = await api.GameInstance.GetTransactionSystem(game.instance);
await shop.GiveItem(player, await api.MarketSystem.Money(), 100); // 100 eddies[/code]
[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]REDagent: an AI modder in the game[/color][/b][/size]
REDagent, powered by Claude, is a chat window in the game that writes REDnode mods with you, starts them, reads their logs, looks at the screen, and fixes what went wrong, while you play. Other mods can ask it questions too. It is a separate download from its [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDagent]repo[/url] and uses your own Anthropic API key.
REDnode also has an MCP server, so Claude Code on your desktop can read your mods' logs, see the overlay's windows, look up game types and call the game.

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792183544-1962604485.png[/img]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Hot reload[/color][/b][/size]
Save your mod's file while the game runs and the mod restarts with the change. No game restart, no save reload.

[b][color=#00ffff][size=4]Performance GPU Sharing[/size][/color]
[/b]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792183728-887783471.png[/img]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Spaces[/color][/b][/size]
Sort windows into named spaces, like virtual desktops, and switch between them with the launcher or Ctrl+1 to 9. REDnode's own tools show in every space.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Mod Manager[/color][/b][/size]
Every REDnode package in one table: switch it on or off, pin it to the launcher or the HUD, move it to a space, and grant or take back what it asks for (the AI assistant, the game's files, staying on top). If a package needs another mod (Codeware, TweakXL, ArchiveXL...), it says which, and whether you have it.

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792182783-77381118.png[/img]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Your own sounds[/color][/b][/size]
Play WAV, OGG, MP3 and FLAC files from your mod, with no soundbank and no REDmod. They follow the game's volume sliders, pause in menus, fade, loop and pan.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]TweakDB, read and changed[/color][/b][/size]
Read any record from the running game, and change it through TweakXL, the community standard, so your changes sit beside every other TweakXL mod. When your mod stops, its changes are undone.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Things in the world[/color][/b][/size]
Spawn entities with meshes and components, move them and remove them, and hear when they attach and detach (with Codeware). This is what EDGEbuilder, a world builder in the game, is made from.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]A debugger in the game[/color][/b][/size]
Turn on Developer mode and open Chromium's DevTools on any window or Node mod, as a window in the game: breakpoints, the console, the network, the page.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]A UI kit in the HUD style[/color][/b][/size]
Buttons, toggles, sliders, tabs, menus, tooltips and scrollbars that look like the game, in two themes. Or build a window with no HTML at all, from Node:

[code]import { game, ui } from 'rednode';

const where = ui.text('Waiting for the game...');
ui.window({ title: 'Hello mod', children: [ui.heading('Where is V'), where] });

setInterval(async () => {
  const p = await game.player.position();
  where.set({ text: `X ${p.x.toFixed(1)}  Y ${p.y.toFixed(1)}  Z ${p.z.toFixed(1)}` });
}, 1000);[/code]
[img width=884]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35355/35355-1792183359-417269450.png[/img]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What is in the download[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The plugin, its scripts, and the overlay host.[/*]
[*]The built-in tools: the launcher, the Mod log and the Mod Manager.[/*]
[*]Six samples, all switched off until you turn them on in the launcher: [b]Hello mod[/b] (a window from Node), [b]Ask mod[/b] (a mod asking the AI assistant), [b]UI kit[/b] (every widget), [b]Vitals[/b] and [b]Coords[/b] (HUD widgets) and [b]Perf[/b] (what the overlay costs).[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit. Tested on game version 2.31.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url] (1.30 or later): loads the plugin.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]: compiles the plugin's scripts.[/*]
[*]Only for the packages that ask for them: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url] (things in the world), [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4197]TweakXL[/url] (TweakDB changes), [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4198]ArchiveXL[/url]. The Mod Manager tells you when one is missing.[/*]
[*]Only for packages that read the game's files: REDbridge. Install [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEdeck]EDGEdeck[/url] and press [b]Get REDbridge[/b], or let [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35356]REDcode[/url] download it. REDnode finds their copy; it is not in this download.[/*]
[/list]
REDnode works beside Cyber Engine Tweaks, other RED4ext plugins, redscript mods and REDmod.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] Mod Manager Download, then enable and deploy.[/*]
[*][b]EDGEdeck:[/b] add the zip, switch it on, deploy.[/*]
[*][b]By hand:[/b] extract the zip into the game folder, so that [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/REDnode.dll[/i] is next to the other RED4ext plugins.[/*]
[/list]
Start the game and press [b]F10[/b]. The first press makes the overlay take the mouse and keyboard, the second hides it, the third shows it again. [b]Esc[/b] gives the mouse back to the game. The [b]REDNODE[/b] tab at the lower left is the launcher.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] remove the mod in your mod manager, or delete [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode[/i]. Your settings are kept in [i]%APPDATA%\@rednode\overlay[/i]; delete that folder too for a clean slate.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Making a REDnode mod[/color][/b][/size]

A REDnode mod is a folder with a [b]rednode-app.json[/b] and either a web page (an app) or a JavaScript file (a Node mod), in [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/[/i]. Publish it on Nexus with that path inside your zip, and list REDnode as a requirement.

[list]
[*][url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/overlay-apps.html]Guide with tested examples[/url]: your first app, windows, HUD widgets, sounds, the game API, TweakDB, the world, debugging.[/*]
[*][url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/api/]API reference[/url] for the rednode package.[/*]
[*][url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/game/]Game API reference[/url]: every class, struct, enum and function in the base game.[/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/tree/main/packages/overlay/apps]Samples[/url], including the ones in this download.[/*]
[/list]
