[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Roadmap[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Overlay[/b]: windows, the UI kit, apps, HUD widgets, GPU sharing, Node mods with the game API, the Mod Manager, the debugger, layers and spaces. Done.[/*]
[*][b]REDagent[/b]: chat, authoring, a picture of the game, mods asking the assistant. Done.[/*]
[*][b]World API[/b] and [b]TweakDB API[/b]: done. TweakDB reads without the game running come next, through REDbridge.[/*]
[*][b]Sound API[/b]: your own files in the game, done. [color=#19f3ff]Next:[/color] sound placed in the world, on entities and positions; then effects, voices and game sound events.[/*]
[*][b]Console[/b]: a console in the game for free-form JavaScript with the whole rednode package ready. Proposed.[/*]
[*][b]Display[/b]: the overlay right in HDR, with frame generation, on ultrawide screens and across resolution and window-mode changes. Planned.[/*]
[*][b]Interceptors[/b]: small scripts that change the game's own functions as they run, inside the game. Planned.[/*]
[/list]
The full table, with every in-game test: [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/]REDnode docs[/url].

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Do I need to install Node.js?[/b]
No. The overlay host brings its own.

[b]Does it slow the game down?[/b]
Very little when nothing is drawn, and a window that does not change costs almost nothing. The Perf sample shows the game's frame rate and the overlay's own time per frame, so you can see for yourself.

[b]Can a broken mod crash my game?[/b]
Node mods run outside the game, in their own processes. A mod that crashes is logged and started again (and left stopped if it keeps crashing); the game and the other mods go on.

[b]Is the AI assistant free?[/b]
REDagent uses your own Anthropic API key, so each answer costs you a little, paid to Anthropic. Nothing is charged by EDGEmodders, and REDnode works without it.

[b]Why is the download so big?[/b]
The overlay host carries its own copy of Chromium and Node (Electron), so it draws pages exactly as a browser does and needs nothing else installed.

[b]Single-player only?[/b]
Yes. Cyberpunk 2077 is a single-player game, and REDnode is for single-player modding.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license. The code is on [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]GitHub[/url].

